[ti:Day 15]

[00:00.00]clause 例 We should include an arbitration clause in the contract. 我们应该在合同中加入仲裁条款。
[00:07.68]scam 例 There is fortunately no need for new regulat ions to crack down on such irresponsible lending practices. 幸运的是，不需 要用新规定来制裁这种不负责任的贷款行为。
[00:20.67]float 例 The new currency would float to a lower level against the Euro. 新货币兑欧元将会浮动到 一个较低的水平。
[00:28.77]refrain 例 Please refrain from smoking and talking loudly during the meeting. 开会期间，请不要抽 烟，不要大声喧哗。
[00:37.85]lean 例 This lean project cut down the company's gross income. 这个收益差的项目拉低了公司的 总收入。
[00:44.98]exploit 例 It's recommended to exploit the particular advantages of each region. 发挥各地独特优势 的策略备受推崇。
[00:54.48]guideline 例 Our guideline is to complement each other's advantages. 我们的方针是优势互补。
[01:02.58]illusion 例 The capacity to modify the economy proved to be an illusion. 事实证明，这种对经济 进行“修正”的能力是痴人说梦。
[01:10.82]far-flung 例 All EU countries are now linked by exchanges, markets and supply routes to diverse and far-flung places. 目前所有欧盟国家 都因贸易交流、市场和供应线路而与遥远的各个 地方联系在一起。
[01:24.51]agribusiness 例 What is the main organisation defect of agribusiness? 农业综合经营的主要体制缺陷是什 么？
[01:32.76]vain 例 I read the scheme again and again, trying hard to understand what he intended to do but in vain. 我一遍又一遍地翻看方案，试图弄清 他的意图，却百思不得其解。
[01:44.35]encounter 例 Let the manager know whenever you encounter any difficulty. 遇到任何困难都要及时 向经理汇报。
[01:52.87]backhander 例 Walmart has been accused of paying backhanders to speed up the opening of new stores. 沃尔玛被指控为加快新店开张的速度而进 行贿赂。
[02:04.33]caution 例 All reports emanating from that country should be treated with caution. 所有来自那个国 家的报告都应谨慎处理。
[02:13.97]model 例 The company is trying to research and develop a new model. 这家公司正在研发一种新 的模型。
[02:21.51]amorphous 例 They are amorphous entities with scant leadership structure or formal process for making decisions. 他们是无组织的实体，缺乏领 导结构和决策的正式过程。
[02:34.92]gazump 例 It is common to be gazumped by proprietors during the property boom. 在房地 产繁荣时期，被业主抬价敲诈的情况很常见。
[02:43.86]destocking 例 Destocking by retailers should be to blame for their poor financial results. 零售商储量缩减 要归咎于他们糟糕的财政状况。
[02:54.48]contemplate 例 Only in extreme circumstances would European leaders contemplate this step. 欧洲 领导人只有在极端情况下才会考虑这一步。
[03:05.38]entangle 例 It's said that the company got entangled in dishonest business dealings. 据说该公司陷入了 进行欺诈性商务操作的丑闻。
[03:15.30]hysteria 例 The hysteria that China might endanger the global economy is overstated. 有关中国可能危 及全球经济的恐慌有些被夸大了。
[03:25.21]pacesetter 例 Beijing has been the pacesetter in implementing tough emission standards over the past decade. 在过去的十年里，北京一直是 严格执行排放标准的领跑者。
[03:38.07]zenith 例 He has not yet reached the zenith of his career. 他还没有达到事业巅峰期。
[03:44.49]cabin 例 All commercial airlines allow a limited number of small pets to fly in the cabin. 所有 的商业航空公司只允许一定数量的小型宠物被带 入机舱。
[03:54.69]fitting 例 For the owner of the fishery, the government offered him a fitting position in a firm. 对于渔场的主人，政府给他在一家公司安排 了一个适合的职位。
[04:05.73]alliance 例 To reduce the transaction cost, the two enterprises came into an alliance as a result of negotiations. 为减少交易费用，这两家企业经 过协商后结成了联盟。
[04:19.00]handsome 例 They made a handsome profit on the property. 他们从这份地产中赚取了丰厚的利润。
[04:25.42]clarity 例 Whatever the screen size, what struck me was not the sharpness of the picture but the clarity of the interface. 无论屏幕有多大，该产 品给我留下深刻印象的不是画面的清晰度，而是 界面的清楚明了。
[04:39.39]analogy 例 There is a fairly good analogy between foreign exchange markets and stock markets. 外汇市场与股票市场非常相似。
[04:50.29]bonanza 例 With the exhaustion of mineral resources, the prospect of finding a bonanza dwindled. 随着矿产资源的枯竭，找到富矿带的希望越来越 小。
[05:01.61]refine 例 The engineers in the information technology department spent many months refining the software. 信息技术部门的工程师们 花费数月改进了软件。
[05:14.18]intense 例 The competition has become increasingly intense for the youths to enter the best enterprises. 年轻人进知名企业的竞争已变得越来 越激烈。
[05:26.47]allay 例 The government is seeking to allay people's fears of economic recession. 政府正在努力缓 解人们对经济衰退的恐惧。
[05:35.97]addendum 例 Any addendum to be agreed in future will be regarded as an integral part of this contract. 今后商定的任何附件都将作为此合同的 一部分。
[05:47.57]biennial 例 The biennial art show which is held in the city is liked by the people. 这个城市每两年举行 一次的艺术展深受人们喜爱。
[05:56.79]access 例 If you can find some data that is reliable and that few other people have access to, you can probably create some very valuable setups for your trading. 如果能发现一些可信、 他人又很难获得的数据，你就有可能制订一些非 常有价值的业务方案。
[06:15.23]tactic 例 Trade barriers are in fact a delaying tactic rather than a real solution. 设置贸易壁垒实际上 是缓兵之计，并不能真正解决问题。
[06:24.73]brisk 例 Business is always brisk before Christmas. 圣诞节前生意总是很兴隆。
[06:30.74]grovel 例 To bring the company out of the red, he has to grovel to the bank manager for a loan. 为了使公司摆脱赤字，他不得不低声下气地向银 行经理申请贷款。
[06:41.07]empirical 例 We get the conclusion after a lot of empirical research. 我们在大量例证研究的基础 上得出了结论。
[06:49.04]evidence 例 There is much evidence to show that the financial crisis has passed. 种种迹象表明，金 融危机已经结束。
[06:58.26]notarise 例 No notary office would notarise this contract as the contents of it are against the law. 没有公证处会公正这份合同，因为它的内容 是违法的。
[07:09.71]headquarters 例 The company's headquarters are based in Hong Kong. 这家公司的总部设在香港。
[07:17.53]mingle 例 You'd better mingle with the colleagues who can help you get ahead. 你最好与那些能帮 助你取得进步的同事交往。
[07:26.34]neutral 例 Keeping a neutral monetary stance is helpful to maintain rapid economic growth. 保 持中立的货币政策对维持经济快速增长有利。
[07:36.95]framework 例 The government has created the framework for a normal foreign exchange market. 政府已 出台了维持外汇交易市场正常交易的准则
[07:47.71]gigantic 例 Their firm is extremely competitive since they have both highly qualified talents and a gigantic and very refined apparatus. 他们公司 极具竞争力，这是由于他们既拥有高层次人才， 又配备了庞大精良的设备。
[08:03.77]negligible 例 Domestic tourism demand's contribution to the economic growth is estimated to be negligible. 国内旅游需求对经济增长的贡献据说 可以忽略不计。
[08:16.49]berth 例 The ship went slowly through the dock to the ship berth. 轮船缓缓驶过码头，到达停泊 处。
[08:23.75]dominant 例 If China hopes to build dominant names in the global consumer market, then it needs a very different role model. 如果中国希望在全球 消费市场建立主导品牌，那么它需要扮演不一样 的角色。
[08:38.00]soar 例 House prices soared a further 20 percent last month. 上月，房价又飞涨了20%。
[08:44.85]outsell 例 According to the statistics, digital cameras will outsell film cameras this year. 据统计，今 年数码相机的销量将超过胶卷相机。
[08:55.74]idealise 例 I don't want to idealise my work. 我不想把工 作理想化。
[09:00.77]circulate 例 The big problem arising from LLP must be the creditor protection. 有限责任合伙带来的最 大问题应该是债权人保护问题。
[09:09.85]annuity 例 While you wait for it to bounce back, annuity rates could fall. 在你等待经济反弹的时 候，年金收益率可能已经下调了。
[09:18.23]built-in 例 The built-in sensors of these shoes can communicate with a runner's iPod to track calorie consumption. 这款鞋内嵌的感应器可以
[09:31.64]emission 例 The government decided to increase the emission of the banknotes. 政府决定增加货币 的发行量。
